; equality_index_past_the_maximum: EQUALITY grows the model to cover the
; largest index it was handed, so that index is a model size and
; MAX_ALLOCATION_SIZE = 2^32 - 1 = 4294967295 bounds it.
;
; An index of 4294967295 needs a model of 4294967296 variables, one past
; the maximum, so the grown size is refused with InvalidAllocation. The
; budget is 68719476736 (64 GiB), above the 34359738360-byte growth
; charge, so the charge succeeds and the range check is what decides.
;
; The fault this pins used to be decided by the target. Rust narrowed the
; index with usize::try_from and swallowed the failure, so on wasm32 --
; where pallet-xqvm runs -- an index past a 32-bit width collapsed the
; needed size to zero, charged nothing, and fell through to
; IndexOutOfBounds, while 64-bit Rust and xqvm_py charged the full growth
; and raised MemoryLimitExceeded. Unlike the allocator operand's split,
; that one was reachable at the shipped 1 GiB default budget and not only
; above 32 GiB.
;
; EQUALITY pops penalty then target, and reads its indices and coeffs
; from the two vec registers named in the operands.

PUSH 1
BQMX r0
VECI r1
VECI r2
PUSH 4294967295
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2
PUSH 1
PUSH 1
EQUALITY r0 r1 r2
HALT
